# c2pool D-MINER.7 alert-relay Telegram sidecar config (RELAY node only, e.g. the
# public bootstrap node). Copy to ~/.config/c2pool/alert-relay.env and
#     chmod 600 ~/.config/c2pool/alert-relay.env
# This file holds the bot token: never commit a filled-in copy.
#
# Absolute path to the c2pool scripts/ dir on this node:
C2POOL_ALERT_SCRIPTS=/home/c2pool/c2pool/scripts
# The relay node's alert-relay state dir (printed at node startup as
# "[alert-relay] ARMED ... state=<dir>"): <data-dir>/<net-subdir>/alert_relay
C2POOL_ALERT_STATE_DIR=/home/c2pool/.c2pool/dash/alert_relay
# Telegram Bot API token from @BotFather (read from the environment, never logged):
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# The designated alert GROUP id (REQUIRED; the sidecar refuses to start without
# it). Group ids are negative: -100xxxxxxxxxx for a supergroup, -xxxxxxxxx for a
# basic group; a public channel may be given as @channelname. A positive id is
# a private chat with one user and is refused (the sidecar has an explicit
# --allow-direct-chat override). How to add the bot to the group and read the
# id: docs/design/d-miner-7-p2p-alert-relay.md, section "Telegram group".
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
